## What changed from v1, and the deletion test
- **Hero reader link: back.** Data: 261 clicks, the top homepage element. Kept to one text link so the hero still has one button (Revision 1's "the user is confused" rule).
- **today: moved from 6th to 2nd.** It ranks (position 8.5 for "today's bhagavad gita verse"); "Verse of the day" was the second-most-clicked hero link (54); audio is the highest-engagement action on the homepage. It also shows "one verse a day", half of the product line, before we ask for anything.
- **sources → which-gita.** Same three trust points, re-asked as the question people actually search. Delete it and the ISKCON and AI objections go unanswered again, and the homepage loses its best-converting query. **Kept, renamed.**
- **plan-preview, devices, gita-for, faq, final:** each passes the deletion test as in v1. gita-for has almost no search demand today (8 impressions on anxiety). It stays because it is cheap, it is where reel and Reddit traffic deep-links, and it is the SEO bet; it moves below which-gita and devices.
- **library:** now carries the primary keyword in its H2 and the Hindi callout uses the top Hindi query's wording.

Total body: about 650 words plus FAQ answers (v1: about 860).

## Tracking to add (so the next gate has real conversions)
- `hero_read_gita_cta` keeps its name, for comparison with the 261 baseline.
- New location names: `home_today_play`, `home_which_gita_cta`, `home_which_gita_essay`.
- App Store button: record `$os` on click (already sent) and stop showing it to Android (fixes the 23 dead clicks).
